{
  "id": 234174450,
  "iid": 11312,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "DHCPFO: Accept empty message digest option",
  "description": "As discussed in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/19178#note_1454063059, this removes \"Message digest is too short\" expert info for empty message digest, as present in Microsoft Windows DHCP server failover setup when message authentication is not configured.\n\nRelated to issue #19178 \n\nSample capture: [dhcpfo.pcapng](/uploads/e6b754a3b3c29ad749c635600a0bd2a1/dhcpfo.pcapng) (requires Wireshark 4.1.0rc0-3053 or later due to payload offset change)\n\nOutput after this change:\n\n```\n        DHCP Style Option, message-digest (17), type not allowed\n            Option Code: message-digest (17)\n            Length: 1\n            Message digest type: Unknown (2)\n                [Expert Info (Warning/Protocol): Message digest type: 2, not allowed]\n                    [Message digest type: 2, not allowed]\n                    [Severity level: Warning]\n                    [Group: Protocol]\n            Message digest: \n```\n\nThe message digest is empty and it can be dragged to display filter (`dhcpfo.messagedigest == \"\"`).",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2023-07-03T07:40:21.509Z",
